• Share login credentials with any other person or organization.
• Sell, rent, reproduce, or distribute our content or materials.
• Reverse-engineer or tamper with security or system infrastructure.
• Integrate DOT Council's materials into your own offerings, services, or courses.
• Conduct system scans or penetration testing without written authorization.
• Remove or modify any copyright, ownership, or trademark notices.

Violations may lead to immediate suspension or termination of your access.`},{id:"ownership",title:"3. Ownership and Intellectual Property",content:"All digital content, software, system designs, written materials, videos, graphics, branding, and documentation used or provided by DOT Council are the property of DOT Council LLC or its licensors. These materials are protected under U.S. and international intellectual property laws. No ownership rights are transferred through this Agreement. Use of DOT Council's name, logos, or materials outside this Agreement requires express written consent."},{id:"duration",title:"4. Course Duration and Access",content:"Each course, training, or compliance program you purchase remains valid for one (1) year from the purchase date unless otherwise specified. After expiration, your access will automatically terminate. Licenses are tied to the individual or business account and may not be reassigned or extended. DOT Council may update or retire courses at any time without prior notice."},{id:"termination",title:"5. Termination and Account Suspension",content:"DOT Council reserves the right to suspend or terminate your access if you violate any term of this Agreement. Termination due to non-compliance will not qualify for a refund. You may also voluntarily discontinue service by emailing support@dotcouncil.com. Sections related to ownership, disclaimers, limitations, and arbitration remain in effect after termination."},{id:"thirdparty",title:"6. Third-Party Content",content:"Some Services may utilize third-party resources or tools. You must adhere to those providers' separate terms and conditions. DOT Council disclaims responsibility for third-party content or its accuracy."},{id:"accuracy",title:"7. Accuracy and Updates",content:"While DOT Council strives to ensure all training and compliance information is accurate and up to date, regulatory requirements may change over time. Our materials serve educational and reference purposes and should not replace official legal or professional advice."},{id:"warranty",title:"8. Warranty Disclaimer",content:'All Services are provided on an "as-is" and "as-available" basis. DOT Council makes no warranties, express or implied, regarding accuracy, reliability, or suitability for a particular purpose. We do not guarantee uninterrupted access or that Services will meet all business needs. Completion of a DOT Council course or program does not guarantee job placement or certification approval.'},{id:"liability",title:"9. Limitation of Liability",content:"To the fullest extent permitted by law, DOT Council shall not be liable for any indirect, incidental, or consequential damages, including business losses or data loss. The maximum liability for any claim shall not exceed the amount paid for the specific Service or course related to the claim."},{id:"governing",title:"10. Governing Law",content:"This Agreement is governed by the laws of the State of Wyoming, United States, without regard to conflict-of-law principles. Any dispute will be resolved under applicable U.S. federal or state law."},{id:"dispute",title:"11. Dispute Resolution and Arbitration",content:"All disputes arising from this Agreement or your use of Services will be resolved by binding arbitration instead of court proceedings, except claims suitable for small claims court. Class actions or group claims are not permitted. Arbitration will comply with the Federal Arbitration Act and be conducted by a neutral arbitrator. You may opt out of arbitration within 30 days of accepting these Terms by contacting support@dotcouncil.com."},{id:"renewal",title:"12. Automatic Renewal",content:"If you enroll in auto-renewal Services, your payment method will be automatically charged at renewal intervals. You may cancel renewal before your next billing date via your account settings."},{id:"modifications",title:"13. Modifications to Terms",content:"DOT Council may modify these Terms at any time. Any updates will appear on our website. Continued use after modifications take effect constitutes agreement to the new Terms."},{id:"communication",title:"14. Communication Consent",content:"By submitting your phone number or email, you consent to receive SMS, WhatsApp messages, calls, and emails from DOT Council about service updates, compliance reminders, or promotional offers. Message frequency may vary. You may unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or emailing support@dotcouncil.com. DOT Council will never share your contact information with third parties."},{id:"privacy",title:"15. Privacy Policy",content:"Use of the Services is governed by our Privacy Policy available at dotcouncil.org. By using our Services, you consent to our data collection and usage practices described therein."},{id:"support",title:"16. Support and Grievance",content:"For any concerns, disputes, or service-related issues, please contact us at support@dotcouncil.com with a detailed explanation. Our support team will review your request and strive for a fair resolution."},{id:"refund",title:"17. Refund and Cancellation Policy",content:`Refund eligibility depends on the following conditions:

• Request made within 72 hours of purchase.
• No certification exam attempted or certificate issued.
• Less than 50% of the course completed.
• No training kits or materials shipped.

Approved refunds are processed back to the original payment method within 10 business days.`},{id:"government",title:"18. No Government Affiliation Disclaimer",content:"DOT Council LLC is a privately owned compliance service provider and is not affiliated, associated, authorized, endorsed by, or in any way connected with any U.S. Department of Transportation (DOT), federal, or state government authority. All compliance support, registration assistance, and training services offered through dotcouncil.org are independent professional services designed to help motor carriers and transportation businesses maintain regulatory readiness."}];return r.jsx("div",{className:"min-h-screen pt-35 bg-gray-50 py-12 px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8",children:r.jsxs("div",{className:"max-w-4xl mx-auto",children:[r.jsxs("div",{className:"bg-white rounded-lg shadow-md p-8 mb-8",children:[r.jsx("div",{className:"flex items-center justify-center mb-4",children:r.jsx(T2,{className:"text-[#1E40AF] text-5xl"})}),r.jsx("h1",{className:"text-4xl font-bold text-center text-gray-900 mb-4",children:"Terms & Conditions"}),r.jsx("p",{className:"text-center text-gray-600 mb-6",children:"Last Updated: October 25, 2025"}),r.jsx("div",{className:"border-t border-gray-200 pt-6",children:r.jsxs("p",{className:"text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed",children:[`This document ("Agreement") outlines the terms between you ("User", "You") and DOT Council LLC ("DOT Council", "We", "Our", "Us"). By accessing or using any of DOT Council's services, platforms, training programs, compliance systems, or materials through dotcouncil.org (collectively, the "Services"), you agree to the following terms and conditions.`," ",r.jsx("span",{className:"font-semibold",children:"If you do not agree, please discontinue use immediately."})," ","This Agreement includes limitations of liability, dispute resolution terms, and other provisions affecting your legal rights."]})})]}),r.jsx("div",{className:"space-y-4",children:u.map(m=>r.jsxs(