hildren:"By continuing to use DOT Council services, you acknowledge that you have read, understood, and agree to be bound by these Terms & Conditions."})})]})})},Qg=()=>{const[s,c]=L.useState({}),o=m=>{c(h=>({...h,[m]:!h[m]}))},u=[{id:"information",title:"1. Information We Collect",content:`We may collect the following categories of information from you:

a. Personal Details:
Name, business name, email address, phone number, and postal/billing address.

b. Account Information:
Login credentials, user IDs, and profile details created while registering or purchasing our services.

c. Payment Data:
Transaction details such as billing address and payment confirmations (processed securely through third-party payment providers — DOT Council does not store credit card details).

d. Usage and Technical Data:
IP address, browser type, device identifiers, operating system details, and browsing behavior for analytics and security purposes.

e. Communications:
Any messages, support requests, feedback, or correspondence shared with our support team.`},{id:"usage",title:"2. How We Use Your Information",content:`DOT Council uses your information only for legitimate business and service-related purposes, including:

• Providing compliance services, training, and account management.
• Processing payments and issuing receipts.
• Sending service updates, registration confirmations, and reminders.
• Responding to inquiries and providing customer support.
• Improving service quality and website functionality through analytics.
• Sending regulatory, promotional, or educational content (if you've opted in).
• Preventing fraud, ensuring data security, and enforcing our Terms & Conditions.`},{id:"sharing",title:"3. Data Sharing and Third Parties",content:`We do not sell or rent your data. However, DOT Council may share necessary information with:

Payment Processors: To complete your authorized payment transactions.

Service Providers: Trusted vendors assisting in operations like hosting, analytics, and communications.

Legal Authorities: When required by law, court orders, or government regulations.

All third-party partners follow strict data protection agreements and are only given the information essential for their purpose.`},{id:"cookies",title:"4. Cookies and Tracking",content:`Our website uses cookies and similar tracking technologies to enhance user experience and analyze website performance. Cookies help remember your preferences and identify returning visitors.

You can disable cookies anytime through your browser settings, though certain features of the website may not function properly without them.`},{id:"security",title:"5. Data Security",content:"We use appropriate administrative, technical, and physical safeguards to protect your personal data from unauthorized access, modification, or disclosure. This includes encrypted transmission (SSL), firewalls, and limited data access. However, no system is completely secure, and you acknowledge using the internet carries inherent risks."},{id:"retention",title:"6. Data Retention",content:"We retain your personal information as long as necessary to fulfill the purposes described in this Privacy Policy, comply with legal requirements, or resolve disputes. Once no longer required, we securely delete or anonymize the data."},{id:"rights",title:"7. Your Rights",content:`Depending on your jurisdiction, you may have the following rights:

• Request access to your personal data.
• Correct or update inaccurate information.
• Request deletion of your data ("Right to be Forgotten").
• Withdraw consent for marketing or communication messages.
• Object to certain types of processing.

Requests can be sent to support@dotcouncil.org. We may require identity verification before processing your request.`},{id:"children",title:"8. Children's Privacy",content:"DOT Council's website and services are not intended for individuals under 13 years of age. We do not knowingly collect personal data from minors. If you believe a child has submitted information, please contact support@dotcouncil.org for immediate removal."},{id:"international",title:"9. International Data Transfers",content:"DOT Council may process and store data in the United States or other locations where we operate. By using our services, you consent to the transfer of your data outside your country, subject to appropriate data protection measures."},{id:"thirdparty",title:"10. Third-Party Links",content:"Our website may include links to external websites not operated by DOT Council. We are not responsible for their privacy practices or content. Please review those sites' privacy policies independently."},{id:"updates",title:"11. Policy Updates",content:"We may revise this Privacy Policy from time to time to reflect legal changes or updates to our business processes. The latest version will always be available on dotcouncil.org. Material updates will be communicated via email or notice on our website."},{id:"contact",title:"12. Contact Information",content:`For questions, requests, or concerns about this Privacy Policy, contact us at:

DOT Council LLC
Phone: (307) 429-4946
Email: support@dotcouncil.org
Website: https://dotcouncil.org
